{
  "title": "Acquired Spastic Equinovarus Deformity",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7000/acquired-spastic-equinovarus-deformity",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 30 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Acquired Spastic Equinovarus Deformity is a progressive foot deformity most commonly seen in patients following a cerebrovascular accident or traumatic brain injury.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with presence of a spastic equinovarus foot deformity in a patient with a prior CVA or TBI.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is an initial trial of observation with bracing. Surgical management is indicated for fixed contractures that persist after the period of neurologic recovery and are not braceable.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**equinus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "secondary to overactivity of the gastrocnemius-soleus complex",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**varus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "due to relative overactivity of the tibialis anterior, with lesser contributions from the FHL, FDL, and tibialis posterior.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Etiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**cerebrovascular accident** (CVA)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**traumatic brain injury** (TBI)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "joint contractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hyperextension of knee in stance phase",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "deformity and difficulty with gait",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7000/images/equinovarus.jpg",
              "caption": "aquired equinovarus"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common physical finding is spastic equinovarus deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "increased tone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hyperreflexia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP, lateral, oblique of foot and ankle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "physical therapy, injections, orthoses",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "as first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "therapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "focus on stretching and strengthening, maintenance of joint range of motion",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "injections",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "phenol blocks and **botulinum toxin injections** are used",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**AFO**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "should be used while the patient is in bed or wheelchair",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Achilles tendon lengthening with split anterior tibialis tendon transfer (SPLATT)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fixed contractures persist after the period of neurologic recovery and are not braceable.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "functional deficits",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "skin problems secondary to deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "equinus deformity is treated with lengthening of the Achilles tendon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "varus deformity is treated with a split anterior tibialis tendon transfer (SPLATT)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Bridle procedure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**posterior tibialis tendon** is transferred through the interosseous membrane to the dorsum of the foot",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "dual anastomosis to the tendon of the anterior tibial and a rerouted peroneus longus in front of the lateral malleolus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "osteotomies and fusions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "recurrence of deformity despite proper soft tissue procedures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Split anterior tibialis tendon transfer (SPLATT)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7000/images/splatt%203.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7000/images/splatt%202.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often done in conjunction with",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "achilles lengthening (open or percutaneous)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "gastrocnemius recession",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lengthening or dorsal transfer of the posterior tibialis tendon (PTT) may also be necessary",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "the tibialis anterior is split and the lateral half is attached to the cuboid through a drill hole and sutured in place",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Hindfoot valgus**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inadvertent lengthening of PTT can result in over correction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Neurologic recovery can take 6 to 18 months in patients who have had a CVA",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "25% regain normal ambulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "75% regain some level of ambulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "neurologic recovery can take years with TBI",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
